  "summary": "•\tOverall 6 years of experience in all phase of Software Development Lifecycle (SDLC) including Requirement Analysis, prototyping, Proof of Concept, Design, Implementation and Testing with Agile and Scrum.\n•\tExpertise in developing web pages using HTML/HTML5, XML, DHTML CSS/CSS3, SASS, LESS, JavaScript, Angular (2/4/5/7/8), React JS, Redux, JQuery, JSON, Node.js, Ajax, JQUERY Bootstrap.\n•\tProficient in designing and developing Single Page Applications using React, React-Router and React-Redux from scratch.\n•\tDesigned pages using Angular JS Forms, Validations, Modules, Events, Expressions, Directives, Controllers, filters and Http Request.\n•\tProficient in designing and developing Single Page Applications using Angular (2/4/5/7/8) and Angular Material.\n•\tWell Versed in writing application level code to interact with APIs, Web Services using AJAX, JSON and XML.\n•\tExpertise in debugging and troubleshooting the code using Firebug, IE Tester, and Chrome Developer Tools and exposure on compatibility issues with different versions of browsers.\n•\tWorking knowledge with third party web services APIs and Web Services using AJAX and JQUERY.\n•\tExperience in Implementing AWS solutions using EC2, S3, RDS, EBS, Elastic Load Balancer, Auto-scaling groups.\n•\tExperienced in using Angular7 Template directives, Routing and navigation, Components, Services and Data Binding.  \n•\tExperience in using Testing frameworks in Test Driven Development (TDD) such as Protractor, Cucumber, and Selenium.\n•\tExpertise in using IDE tools such as Notepad ++, Web Matrix, Eclipse, Sublime Text Editor, IntelliJ IDEA, and Web Storm.\n•\tAdhere to W3C standards and follow best practices when developing web pages.\n•\tExpertise in RESTful, SOAP web services to integrate between Application to Application\n•\tExperience in Version Control tool GIT and Clear-Case for Source Code version management.\t\n•\tEasily adaptable to the work conditions and consistently deliver the quality work and Capable of adapting to new technologies and can face any new challenge that exist in the project.\n",
